la occur at $(0,\\pm a).$ From the graph, we have that $(0,1)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=1.$\n\nRecall also that the asymptotes of the hyperbola occur at $y=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a}{b} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{b} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ b & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346341 13194139535371 true] [17592186346340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346342 13194139535371 true] [17592186346340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346343 13194139535371 true] [17592186346340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346344 13194139535371 true] [17592186346340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346345 13194139535371 true] [17592186346340 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535371 true] [17592186346340 1041 "selection" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346340 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346341 13194139535371 true] [17592186346340 1110 #uuid "0a424228-f16e-5293-ae53-ee24b73245ea" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346341 1034 "x=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346341 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346341 1111 #uuid "34a5a16f-5e2a-501c-9c05-7d8e3588051a" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346342 1034 "x=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346342 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346342 1111 #uuid "66dfbd48-73e4-5586-9b95-f706d1df1511" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346343 1034 "x=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346343 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346343 1111 #uuid "581020ee-018e-5525-a0a2-1b9c570127dd" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346344 1034 "x=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346344 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346344 1111 #uuid "1afbf06a-297c-5ee2-b9d1-9b797167ac6d" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346345 1034 "x=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346345 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346345 1111 #uuid "d162ca6b-2bb8-5578-b8c5-dd0c935d07e7" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346346 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346347 13194139535371 true] [17592186346346 1089 "q-106620" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346346 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535371 true] [17592186346346 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/assets/e2203c195dbcd9ae474f5d00f00e81d63ec6527c0367e96a8a7520522c967265.png)\n\nFind the parametric equations of the hyperbola shown above given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}x.$" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346346 1113 #uuid "fc8cdff2-ffdf-55ed-95c0-18e8793dab2e" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346346 1145 "The parametric equations of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by \n\n$$\nx=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(0,\\pm a).$ From the graph, we have that $(0,-3)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=3.$\n\nRecall also that the asymptotes of the hyperbola occur at $y=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a}{b} & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{b} & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ b & =\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346347 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346348 13194139535371 true] [17592186346347 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346349 13194139535371 true] [17592186346347 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346350 13194139535371 true] [17592186346347 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346351 13194139535371 true] [17592186346347 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346352 13194139535371 true] [17592186346347 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535371 true] [17592186346347 1041 "selection" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346347 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346348 13194139535371 true] [17592186346347 1110 #uuid "0325bf50-412d-5f7e-97f1-96cdf824d0c1" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346348 1034 "x=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346348 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346348 1111 #uuid "0278f54d-318a-5abd-908b-a4eccdb8622e" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346349 1034 "x=5\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=9\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346349 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346349 1111 #uuid "e3f43754-8c54-53af-9947-b183e5faae90" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346350 1034 "x=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346350 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346350 1111 #uuid "588169c4-5db7-5588-8399-debaa184ee9c" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346351 1034 "x=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346351 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346351 1111 #uuid "24880b86-4cae-5b70-a80e-144502a0e917" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346352 1034 "x=5\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=9\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346352 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346352 1111 #uuid "3efa7b90-80b1-5171-83e9-23663b93924d" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346353 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346354 13194139535371 true] [17592186346353 1089 "q-106626" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346353 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535371 true] [17592186346353 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.$" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346353 1113 #uuid "90c35775-1aa2-582d-b3c4-a5b63abcbbe4" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346353 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent Identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{\\sqrt{3}} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{3} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+1 & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346354 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346355 13194139535371 true] [17592186346354 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346356 13194139535371 true] [17592186346354 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346357 13194139535371 true] [17592186346354 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346358 13194139535371 true] [17592186346354 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346359 13194139535371 true] [17592186346354 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535371 true] [17592186346354 1041 "selection" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346354 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346357 13194139535371 true] [17592186346354 1110 #uuid "a275f630-037e-5c2a-b416-95dfc6080918" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346355 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346355 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346355 1111 #uuid "b21a5be1-6e5a-59c8-af9c-1a0b5dd3bc41" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346356 1034 "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}=1" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346356 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346356 1111 #uuid "538f8d72-22bf-5604-9112-99f278e54506" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346357 1034 "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}=1" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346357 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346357 1111 #uuid "9fe8d6f1-4f0f-52db-a90e-ab67b237daa2" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346358 1034 "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}=1" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346358 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346358 1111 #uuid "b9786096-ec20-56cc-ba5a-a3c6aacf4893" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346359 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346359 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346359 1111 #uuid "d4af1a68-b060-567a-ae00-36d818ee9615" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346360 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346361 13194139535371 true] [17592186346360 1089 "q-106671" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346360 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535371 true] [17592186346360 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=8\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.$" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346360 1113 #uuid "f1efecd9-c3e6-54d4-a6a0-6af38953777c" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346360 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent Identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =8\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{8} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{8}^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{64} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Squaring the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =5\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{5} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}+1 & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{64} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346361 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346362 13194139535371 true] [17592186346361 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346363 13194139535371 true] [17592186346361 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346364 13194139535371 true] [17592186346361 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346365 13194139535371 true] [17592186346361 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346366 13194139535371 true] [17592186346361 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535371 true] [17592186346361 1041 "selection" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346361 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346366 13194139535371 true] [17592186346361 1110 #uuid "a321b7b9-3f1e-5e55-8686-a575a39afa87" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346362 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{64}=1" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346362 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346362 1111 #uuid "61998645-3741-53ab-8927-a497ce1cbd5f" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346363 1034 "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}=1" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346363 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346363 1111 #uuid "7eceaa67-e4ff-52bc-9ade-65aa1f009f71" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346364 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346364 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346364 1111 #uuid "952863ea-7c16-5ce0-8530-8271bc15b34c" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346365 1034 "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{64}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}=1" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346365 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346365 1111 #uuid "4a625f29-b3b1-5f2f-a1e1-5e29b15a2f6f" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346366 1034 "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}=1" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346366 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346366 1111 #uuid "6970ed7d-90dc-5363-a471-850dc615ecf2" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346367 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346368 13194139535371 true] [17592186346367 1089 "q-106682" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346367 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535371 true] [17592186346367 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/assets/ab11a3dde0aebbd4088c498e37da48909f9a309ca9d4ab29bfcfa788d53e5c5e.png)\n\nOne branch of a hyperbola (shown above) is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $t?$" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346367 1113 #uuid "5fe995fe-d9fb-57f1-81bc-8d7ca13c35e7" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346367 1145 "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a single branch, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/assets/f825ca9f9431ca38b14ed141639d5cf4189f0fde0526e943ddb956e112c3e4ab.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $[-\\pi ,-\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and $(\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ],$ we get only the lower branch.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe only the lower branch are\n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,-\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\cup (\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ].\n$$" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346368 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346369 13194139535371 true] [17592186346368 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346370 13194139535371 true] [17592186346368 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346371 13194139535371 true] [17592186346368 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346372 13194139535371 true] [17592186346368 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346373 13194139535371 true] [17592186346368 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535371 true] [17592186346368 1041 "selection" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346368 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346372 13194139535371 true] [17592186346368 1110 #uuid "161b36d7-587e-5c40-a2b5-a00cf3315381" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346369 1034 "t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346369 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346369 1111 #uuid "df3a649c-124d-535c-a595-7ddf961707a5" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346370 1034 "t\\in [0,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346370 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346370 1111 #uuid "9d44f8a8-171a-5f9a-b253-dea04c59a2e5" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346371 1034 "t\\in [-\\pi ,0],\\,t\\ne -\\frac{\\pi }{2}" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346371 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346371 1111 #uuid "de94a279-5292-51ae-b81b-55109917d031" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346372 1034 "t\\in [-\\pi ,-\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\cup (\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ]" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346372 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346372 1111 #uuid "b5149c80-0510-5472-b9a6-0e2b784675fa" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346373 1034 "t\\in (-\\frac{3\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2})" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346373 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346373 1111 #uuid "5d2bee71-093b-5afb-8894-bc126721dc12" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346374 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346375 13194139535371 true] [17592186346374 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346377 13194139535371 true] [17592186346374 1089 "q-275792" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346374 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535371 true] [17592186346374 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/assets/20138a518801a1bac0a76303a86d6ca4b2fe289f5dae230517730f7398de3945.png)\n\nComplete the following parametric equations generating the hyperbola above in terms of the parameter $t,$ defined for $t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ where $t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{4}{5}x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346374 1113 #uuid "5c73b5f1-13f8-5d58-9924-2732adfaffbc" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346374 1145 "The parametric equations of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by \n\n$$\nx=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(0,\\pm a).$ From the graph, we have that $(0,4)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=4.$\n\nRecall also that the asymptotes of the hyperbola occur at $y=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{4}{5}x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a}{b} & =\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{b} & =\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ b & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346375 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346376 13194139535371 true] [17592186346375 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535371 true] [17592186346375 1041 "field-1" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346375 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346376 13194139535371 true] [17592186346375 1110 #uuid "fe5368bc-e1e1-50eb-9eac-2b5d739feafb" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346376 1034 "5\\tan(t)" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346376 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346376 1111 #uuid "ff92f23b-c5fc-5780-9d67-12a377e8284b" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346377 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346378 13194139535371 true] [17592186346377 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535371 true] [17592186346377 1041 "field-2" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346377 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346378 13194139535371 true] [17592186346377 1110 #uuid "a71d719c-bae2-5673-af1c-680218afe7d1" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346378 1034 "4" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346378 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535371 true] [17592186346378 1111 #uuid "c87358ea-65e8-5e8e-8430-96d83b5ed9a7" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346379 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346380 13194139535371 true] [17592186346379 1089 "q-275794" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346379 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535371 true] [17592186346379 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$=1$" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346379 1113 #uuid "3ae69cc2-2076-5c1c-92eb-0c5855f63441" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346379 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent Identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{3} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{2} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+1 & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535371 true] [17592186346380 1000 #edb/re